{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-B-glm53flash-max-std-full200-20261010","prediction_set_name":"glm53flash-max-std-full200-20261010","paper_id":"2505.07765","judge_input_sha256":"fe99960043afac54b2a8c9e825ab597b702b55fdead8cce4eb12b8386ef18dae","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2505.07765:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2505.07765:I001:U002","2505.07765:I001:U003","2505.07765:I001:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is a wrong coefficient rescaling in the finite random-feature regularizer, including the N-dependence and factor induced by c_n=c(omega_n)/N. ISSUE-002 concerns an unsupported Sobolev-density argument and does not identify or repair this finite-objective formula.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2505.07765:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2505.07765:I002:U001","2505.07765:I002:U002","2505.07765:I002:U003","2505.07765:I002:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the missing nonnegativity condition on empirical weights, whose absence permits the objective to tend to minus infinity and defeats existence of a minimizer. ISSUE-002 instead identifies a missing proof of Sobolev density and supplies no diagnosis of signed-weight unboundedness or the required sign condition.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2505.07765:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2505.07765:I003:U001","2505.07765:I003:U002","2505.07765:I003:U003","2505.07765:I003:U004","2505.07765:I003:U005","2505.07765:I003:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U005","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue shows that setwise convergence of finite empirical measures cannot hold for finite-node measures converging to an atomless target, and therefore does not cover the intended quadrature regime. ISSUE-002 addresses density in a Sobolev norm, not the convergence mode, atomic-versus- nonatomic measure obstruction, or its quadrature repair.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2505.07765:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2505.07765:I005:U001","2505.07765:I005:U002","2505.07765:I005:U003","2505.07765:I005:U004","2505.07765:I005:U006","2505.07765:I005:U008"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U002","ISSUE-004:U003","ISSUE-004:U006","ISSUE-004:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the false relative estimate L(v)≤2 hat L(v), caused by finite evaluation kernels, and the need for a uniform additive quadrature bound. ISSUE-004 concerns whether an appendix embedding applies to the restricted dictionary and does not diagnose failure of the relative generalization inequality or provide its additive-error repair.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}